DATA, STANDARDS AND ENGINEERING OUTPUT

Cell, component and standards data
  The data modules contain factual values transcribed from public manufacturer
  datasheets and publicly available standards catalogues, together with this
  project's own curation, classification and notes. The curation is covered by
  the Apache 2.0 licence above. The underlying facts are not claimed as this
  project's property.

  No standard is reproduced in this repository. REFERENCES.md *cites* the
  standards it relies on; the documents themselves must be obtained from the
  issuing bodies (IEC, ISO, UL, NFPA, UNECE, SAC/GB, CEN, IEEE, SAE).

  Customer-supplied cell data never leaves the user's device and is never
  published by this project.

Patent landscape
  The patent module maps designs to families of publicly filed prior art and
  links to Google Patents for orientation only. It is not, and must not be used
  as, a freedom-to-operate opinion.

Engineering output
  This software produces first-order engineering estimates. It is design
  guidance, not certification, and does not replace testing, homologation or
  the judgement of a qualified engineer. Assumptions that have no public source
  are listed openly in REFERENCES.md, section 8.

